On Fri, 25 Jul 2003 22:45:01 -0700, JH wrote:

> Ok, I'm not a unix guru, so the whole patch/diff thing is still a bit of a
> mystery to me, so how do I create the .diff files you use for patches?  I'm
> assuming with diff, but the diff --help isn't so helpful.  What do I do?

Create two directories - one with the original source, and one with the
new source. Remember to delete any temporary files, backups, .o files,
Makefiles, etc.

Then:
diff -Naur nethack-original nethack-new > patch

Then review the patch to make sure you didn't leave anything in that
shouldn't be there.

